/-!
# KFB: Gaussian-integer data on item stacks, linear-combination expressions

* `GI = ℤ × ℤ` (Gaussian integer `a + b i`), stored on a stack as the two items `a, b`
  (`gflat`).  `toC` is the embedding into `ℂ`; `gmul` the product.
* `lcE l`: the register expression `Σ c_t · top(r_t)` for coefficients `c_t ∈ {-1, 0, 1}`, built
